1. Requirements
===============
- USE (downloads available here: http://sourceforge.net/projects/useocl/)

2. Installation
===============
Please, copy the jar-file into the lib/plugins directory of USE.

The Java based solver SAT4j comes with the plugin and needs no installation.

Native solvers are installed by hand, before USE starts. Copy a solver's
library into lib/plugins/modelValidatorPlugin/x64 under the USE directory, or
into lib/plugins/modelValidatorPlugin/x86 for a 32-bit Java. Then start USE
with -Djava.library.path set to that folder, for example in VMARGS in bin/use
or bin/start_use.bat. Name the library after the solver in lower case, as
Java expects on your system: libminisat.so on Linux, libminisat.dylib on
macOS or minisat.dll on Windows for MiniSat, and the same for lingeling,
minisatprover and cryptominisat. The plingeling solver is an executable named
plingeling in the same folder. Select the solver with
`mv -config satsolver:=MiniSat', or `mv -config satsolver:=MiniSat; save' to
keep it. When the plugin cannot load the solver, the command lists the
solvers it can load.

3. Usage
===============
The shell command 'plugins' shows all available Model Validator commands.
For further information, please feel free to use our sourceforge forums. A
quick reference guide is included in the Model Validator ZIP archive.

4. What the translation refuses
===============================
The plugin refuses to validate a model with an expression it cannot
translate faithfully, and names that expression, rather than answer with a
verdict that USE could contradict.

any() is refused. On a Set or Bag with several matching elements, USE
returns the first one its hash-based collection iterates: Set{3, 20}->any(true)
is 20, and objects are placed by the hash of their names. The plugin does not
model that choice, so a translated any() could change a verdict. On a Sequence
or OrderedSet, the message names the order instead. In USE's examples,
Metamodels/UML23/UML2MM.use and Others/Sudoku/Sudoku.use use any(). Where only
the existence of a match or a property of all matches matters,
select(...)->notEmpty() or select(...)->forAll(...) expresses it and is
translated.
